{"id":"g06","name":"Taxi Driver Features","lang":"pyspark","entry":"solve","params":["spark","drivers_df","cars_df","rides_1_df","rides_2_df","rides_3_df","rides_4_df"],"limit_s":30,"ordered":false,"desc":"<p>The taxi company wants one feature row per driver to train a model. Today is <b>2023-04-15</b>.</p>\n<p><code>drivers_df</code>: <code>driver_id</code> int, <code>car_id</code> int, <code>age</code> int (can be null), <code>started_driving_year</code> int, <code>second_language</code> string, <code>rating</code> double, <code>net_worth_of_tips</code> double, <code>driver_class</code> string. Every driver has exactly one car.</p>\n<p><code>cars_df</code>: <code>car_id</code> int, <code>model</code> string, <code>manufacture_year</code> int, <code>last_inspection_date</code> date.</p>\n<p>The rides arrive in four parts <code>rides_1_df</code> to <code>rides_4_df</code> with the same columns: <code>ride_id</code> int, <code>driver_id</code> int, <code>date</code> date, <code>status</code> string, and six booleans <code>car_clearness_upvote_given</code>, <code>politeness_upvote_given</code>, <code>communication_upvote_given</code>, <code>punctuality_upvote_given</code>, <code>complaint_given</code>, <code>incident_occurred</code>.</p>\n<p>Return one row per driver with these columns, in this order:</p>\n<ul><li><code>driver_id</code>;</li>\n<li><code>car_model</code> and <code>car_manufacture_year</code>: the <code>model</code> and <code>manufacture_year</code> of the driver's car;</li>\n<li><code>days_since_inspection</code>: number of calendar days from <code>last_inspection_date</code> to 2023-04-15;</li>\n<li><code>age</code> (unchanged, may stay null);</li>\n<li><code>experience</code>: <code>2023 - started_driving_year</code>;</li>\n<li><code>second_language</code>, <code>rating</code>, <code>net_worth_of_tips</code> (unchanged);</li>\n<li><code>number_of_rejected_rides</code>: rides whose <code>status</code> is exactly <code>\"Rejected by the driver\"</code>;</li>\n<li><code>number_of_upvotes</code>: the total number of <code>true</code> values in the four <code>*_upvote_given</code> columns over all the driver's rides (one ride can give up to 4 upvotes);</li>\n<li><code>number_of_complaints</code>: rides with <code>complaint_given</code> true;</li>\n<li><code>number_of_incidents</code>: rides with <code>incident_occurred</code> true;</li>\n<li><code>driver_class</code> (unchanged).</li></ul>\n<p>The four parts must be combined before counting. A driver with no ride keeps a row, with the four counts equal to <code>0</code>. The row order does not matter.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p><code>drivers_df</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>driver_id</th><th>car_id</th><th>age</th><th>started_driving_year</th><th>second_language</th><th>rating</th><th>net_worth_of_tips</th><th>driver_class</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>11</td><td>35</td><td>2015</td><td>French</td><td>4.6</td><td>120.5</td><td>A class</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>12</td><td>null</td><td>2020</td><td>no</td><td>3.9</td><td>40.0</td><td>B class</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>13</td><td>52</td><td>2001</td><td>English</td><td>4.9</td><td>300.0</td><td>A class</td></tr></table></div><p><code>cars_df</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>car_id</th><th>model</th><th>manufacture_year</th><th>last_inspection_date</th></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>Toyota Prius</td><td>2018</td><td>2023-03-15</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>Dacia Logan</td><td>2014</td><td>2022-12-31</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>Skoda Octavia</td><td>2020</td><td>2023-04-15</td></tr></table></div><p><code>rides_1_df</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>ride_id</th><th>driver_id</th><th>date</th><th>status</th><th>car_clearness_upvote_given</th><th>politeness_upvote_given</th><th>communication_upvote_given</th><th>punctuality_upvote_given</th><th>complaint_given</th><th>incident_occurred</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>2023-04-01</td><td>Success</td><td>true</td><td>true</td><td>false</td><td>true</td><td>false</td><td>false</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2</td><td>2023-04-02</td><td>Rejected by the driver</td><td>false</td><td>false</td><td>false</td><td>false</td><td>false</td><td>false</td></tr></table></div><p><code>rides_2_df</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>ride_id</th><th>driver_id</th><th>date</th><th>status</th><th>car_clearness_upvote_given</th><th>politeness_upvote_given</th><th>communication_upvote_given</th><th>punctuality_upvote_given</th><th>complaint_given</th><th>incident_occurred</th></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>1</td><td>2023-04-03</td><td>Rejected by the driver</td><td>false</td><td>false</td><td>false</td><td>false</td><td>true</td><td>false</td></tr></table></div><p><code>rides_3_df</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>ride_id</th><th>driver_id</th><th>date</th><th>status</th><th>car_clearness_upvote_given</th><th>politeness_upvote_given</th><th>communication_upvote_given</th><th>punctuality_upvote_given</th><th>complaint_given</th><th>incident_occurred</th></tr></table></div><p><code>rides_4_df</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>ride_id</th><th>driver_id</th><th>date</th><th>status</th><th>car_clearness_upvote_given</th><th>politeness_upvote_given</th><th>communication_upvote_given</th><th>punctuality_upvote_given</th><th>complaint_given</th><th>incident_occurred</th></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>2</td><td>2023-04-05</td><td>Rejected by the client</td><td>false</td><td>true</td><td>false</td><td>false</td><td>true</td><td>true</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>1</td><td>2023-04-06</td><td>Success</td><td>true</td><td>true</td><td>true</td><td>true</td><td>false</td><td>false</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>driver_id</th><th>car_model</th><th>car_manufacture_year</th><th>days_since_inspection</th><th>age</th><th>experience</th><th>second_language</th><th>rating</th><th>net_worth_of_tips</th><th>number_of_rejected_rides</th><th>number_of_upvotes</th><th>number_of_complaints</th><th>number_of_incidents</th><th>driver_class</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Toyota Prius</td><td>2018</td><td>31</td><td>35</td><td>8</td><td>French</td><td>4.6</td><td>120.5</td><td>1</td><td>7</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>A class</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Dacia Logan</td><td>2014</td><td>105</td><td>null</td><td>3</td><td>no</td><td>3.9</td><td>40.0</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>B class</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Skoda Octavia</td><td>2020</td><td>0</td><td>52</td><td>22</td><td>English</td><td>4.9</td><td>300.0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>A class</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 30 seconds (pyspark)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 2 GB<br><b>[input]</b> DataFrame drivers_df, cars_df, rides_1_df, rides_2_df, rides_3_df, rides_4_df</div>","starter":"from pyspark.sql import SparkSession, DataFrame, functions as F\n\n\ndef solve(spark: SparkSession, drivers_df: DataFrame, cars_df: DataFrame, rides_1_df: DataFrame,\n          rides_2_df: DataFrame, rides_3_df: DataFrame, rides_4_df: DataFrame) -> DataFrame:\n    # write your code here\n    return drivers_df\n","hints":["Réunis les 4 rides, agrège-les par driver_id, puis fais une jointure GAUCHE depuis drivers : sinon les chauffeurs sans course disparaissent. Ensuite F.coalesce(col, F.lit(0)).","number_of_upvotes additionne les 4 colonnes booléennes : F.sum(F.col(c).cast(\"int\")) pour chacune, puis additionne. days_since_inspection = F.datediff(F.lit(\"2023-04-15\").cast(\"date\"), F.col(\"last_inspection_date\"))."],"summary_fr":"Construire une ligne de features par chauffeur : infos de sa voiture, jours depuis l'inspection, expérience, et 4 compteurs calculés sur ses courses (refus, votes positifs, plaintes, incidents). Un chauffeur sans course garde sa ligne avec des 0.","tags":["union de partitions","jointure gauche","agrégation conditionnelle","dates","zéro si aucune course","BCG"],"minutes":25,"source":"Question rapportée du test BCG (fastprep.io, à l'origine en Pandas), réécrite en PySpark et testée par Kata Lab","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>solution.py</code>.</li><li>Complète la fonction <code>solve(spark, drivers_df, cars_df, rides_1_df, rides_2_df, rides_3_df, rides_4_df)</code>. Garde son nom et ses paramètres : ce sont les tests qui l'appellent, avec leurs propres données. N'écris pas d'appel à la fonction toi-même.</li><li><code>spark</code> est une SparkSession déjà prête : ne crée pas la tienne.</li><li><code>drivers_df</code>, <code>cars_df</code>, <code>rides_1_df</code>, <code>rides_2_df</code>, <code>rides_3_df</code>, <code>rides_4_df</code> sont des DataFrames déjà chargés : ses colonnes sont celles de l'énoncé (onglet <b>Input</b> d'un test pour les voir).</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Ta fonction doit <b>renvoyer</b> le résultat avec <code>return</code>. Un <code>print</code> ou un <code>show()</code> ne compte pas : il sort seulement dans l'onglet <b>Console Output</b>.</li><li>Le DataFrame renvoyé doit avoir <b>exactement 14 colonnes</b>, avec ces noms et dans cet ordre : <code>driver_id</code>, <code>car_model</code>, <code>car_manufacture_year</code>, <code>days_since_inspection</code>, <code>age</code>, <code>experience</code>, <code>second_language</code>, <code>rating</code>, <code>net_worth_of_tips</code>, <code>number_of_rejected_rides</code>, <code>number_of_upvotes</code>, <code>number_of_complaints</code>, <code>number_of_incidents</code>, <code>driver_class</code>. Une colonne en plus (une colonne de calcul oubliée), un nom différent ou un autre ordre et le test est faux, même si les valeurs sont justes. Finis par un <code>select(...)</code> de ces colonnes.</li><li>L'ordre des lignes ne compte pas : les tests trient les deux tables avant de comparer.</li><li>Valeurs : les nombres sont comparés à 0,000001 près : arrondis seulement là où l'énoncé le demande, et au nombre de décimales demandé ; une case vide attendue s'écrit <code>null</code> : ce n'est ni <code>0</code> ni une chaîne vide.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Spark tourne dans ton Codespace : au premier RUN TESTS de la séance, attends qu'il soit prêt (1 à 2 minutes). Ensuite chaque lancement prend quelques secondes.</li><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : tes 2 tests visibles tournent.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 2/2. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 5 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"drivers_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"driver_id int, car_id int, age int, started_driving_year int, second_language string, rating double, net_worth_of_tips double, driver_class string","rows":[[1,11,35,2015,"French",4.6,120.5,"A class"],[2,12,null,2020,"no",3.9,40.0,"B class"],[3,13,52,2001,"English",4.9,300.0,"A class"]]}},"cars_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"car_id int, model string, manufacture_year int, last_inspection_date date","rows":[[11,"Toyota Prius",2018,"2023-03-15"],[12,"Dacia Logan",2014,"2022-12-31"],[13,"Skoda Octavia",2020,"2023-04-15"]]}},"rides_1_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"ride_id int, driver_id int, date date, status string, car_clearness_upvote_given boolean, politeness_upvote_given boolean, communication_upvote_given boolean, punctuality_upvote_given boolean, complaint_given boolean, incident_occurred boolean","rows":[[1,1,"2023-04-01","Success",true,true,false,true,false,false],[2,2,"2023-04-02","Rejected by the driver",false,false,false,false,false,false]]}},"rides_2_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"ride_id int, driver_id int, date date, status string, car_clearness_upvote_given boolean, politeness_upvote_given boolean, communication_upvote_given boolean, punctuality_upvote_given boolean, complaint_given boolean, incident_occurred boolean","rows":[[3,1,"2023-04-03","Rejected by the driver",false,false,false,false,true,false]]}},"rides_3_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"ride_id int, driver_id int, date date, status string, car_clearness_upvote_given boolean, politeness_upvote_given boolean, communication_upvote_given boolean, punctuality_upvote_given boolean, complaint_given boolean, incident_occurred boolean","rows":[]}},"rides_4_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"ride_id int, driver_id int, date date, status string, car_clearness_upvote_given boolean, politeness_upvote_given boolean, communication_upvote_given boolean, punctuality_upvote_given boolean, complaint_given boolean, incident_occurred boolean","rows":[[4,2,"2023-04-05","Rejected by the client",false,true,false,false,true,true],[5,1,"2023-04-06","Success",true,true,true,true,false,false]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["driver_id","car_model","car_manufacture_year","days_since_inspection","age","experience","second_language","rating","net_worth_of_tips","number_of_rejected_rides","number_of_upvotes","number_of_complaints","number_of_incidents","driver_class"],"rows":[[1,"Toyota Prius",2018,31,35,8,"French",4.6,120.5,1,7,1,0,"A class"],[2,"Dacia Logan",2014,105,null,3,"no",3.9,40.0,1,1,1,1,"B class"],[3,"Skoda Octavia",2020,0,52,22,"English",4.9,300.0,0,0,0,0,"A class"]]}},{"input":{"drivers_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"driver_id int, car_id int, age int, started_driving_year int, second_language string, rating double, net_worth_of_tips double, driver_class string","rows":[[9,90,44,2023,"no",4.0,0.0,"B class"]]}},"cars_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"car_id int, model string, manufacture_year int, last_inspection_date date","rows":[[90,"Hyundai Ioniq",2022,"2023-01-01"]]}},"rides_1_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"ride_id int, driver_id int, date date, status string, car_cle